21-04-23T09:31:00.000Z","updated_at":"2022-01-04T04:32:14.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8iyeN56GEhzI4vHMw4Ha8","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8iyeN56GEhzI4vHMw4Ha8"}},{"id":"LnIhKeZCcdOlaZ4hIpAdF","ext":"jpg","post_id":"LnIhKeZCcdOlaZ4hIpAdF","description":"","caption":"Above Moab","poi_name":null,"subject":"Above Moab","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2021-04-23T09:33:00.000Z","updated_at":"2022-01-04T04:33:54.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/LnIhKeZCcdOlaZ4hIpAdF","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/LnIhKeZCcdOlaZ4hIpAdF"}}],"detail":{"id":"1841","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Colorado River through the Professor Valley can begin at the take-out for the popular Westwater Canyon run. The first 24 miles to Hittle Bottom are a mellow Class I float. Some come specifically for this sections while many bypass it by putting in at Hittle Bottom or Dewey Bridge at the Dolores confluence. For those who paddle this first section the absense of others and the presence of wildlife is notable from upstream or downstream.\n\nWhile there's not any real action, a few whitewater rapids (class II/III), do break up the scenic float once you enter the Professor Valley past Hittle Bottom.\n\nThis 18 mile stretch in the middle of the run makes a good overnight trip.\n\nIt IS popular so don't expect to have the river to yourself and camping is restricted to designated sites with roadside ranger enforcement.\n\nBoaters can continue their trip downstream to Cataract Canyon (Permit required past the Green River confluence) or take advantage of boating opportunities on the upstream sections of the Colorado or Dolores which come together just downstream of the Rose Ranch put-in:\n\n- [07) Colorado River, Loma (CO) to Westwater, Horsethief and Ruby Canyon, 27 miles, I-II](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1839/)\n- [08) Colorado River, Westwater to Cisco (Rose Ranch), Westwater Canyon, 17 miles, I-IV](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1840/)\n\n- [1) Dolores River, Bradfield Launch to Dove Creek Pump Station, 19 miles, II-III](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/385/)\n- [2) Dolores River, Dove Creek Pump Station to Slickrock, 28 miles, II-III+(IV)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/386/)\n- [3) Dolores River, Slickrock to Bedrock, 50 miles, II+(III)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/387/)\n- [4) Dolores River, Bedrock to Gateway, 44 miles, II+](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/388/)\n- [5) Dolores River, Gateway to Colorado River below Rose Ranch, 30 miles, II+(IV)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/389/)\n\nOther Reaches of the Colorado River:\n\n[01\\. Hot Sulphur Springs to Hwy 40 bridge (Byers Canyon)](../../content/River_detail_id_377_) (CO, IV)\n\n[02\\. Gore Canyon](../../content/River_detail_id_378_) (CO, IV-V)\n\n[03\\. Pumphouse campground to Rancho Del Rio (Pumphouse)](../../content/River_detail_id_379_) (CO, III)\n\n[04\\. Hanging Lake Exit 125 (I-70) to Shoshone Power Plant Exit 123 (I-70) (Barrel Springs)](../../content/River_detail_id_380_) (CO, IV-V \\[V+\\])\n\n[05\\. Shoshone Power Plant, Exit 123 (I-70) to Grizzly Creek, Exit 121 (I-70) (Shoshone)](../../content/River_detail_id_4260_) (CO, III-IV)\n\n[06\\. Cameo Dam (Big Sur / Lucky 7)](../../content/River_detail_id_4261_) (CO, III)\n\n[07\\. Loma to Westwater (Ruby / Horsethief Canyons)](../../content/River_detail_id_381_) (CO-UT, II)\n\n[08\\. Westwater to Rose Ranch (Westwater Canyon)](../../content/River_detail_id_1840_) (UT, I-IV)\n\n[09\\. Cisco (Rose Ranch) to Moab (Professor Valley)](../../content/River_detail_id_1841_) (UT, I-III)\n\n[10\\. Moab to Powell Reservoir (Cataract Canyon)](../../content/River_detail_id_1842_) (UT, I-IV)\n\n[11\\. Lees Ferry to Lake Mead (Grand Canyon)](../../content/River_detail_id_114_) (AZ, I-V)\n\n[12\\. Black Canyon](../../content/River_detail_id_3190_) (AZ-NV, I)","averageGradient":"5","maxGradient":"0","length":"46.7","correlations":[{"reachID":"1841","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"2000","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"15000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"COLORADO RIVER NEAR CISCO, UT","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"09180500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"2010","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.03","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"38.81054095","longitude":"-109.2934493"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/09180500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/09180500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"2010","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["109650","101495","101500","101501","vJ8odvZ4Oh85DDeOrIvDv","114902"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-109.24939813932029,38.97026005488224],[-109.24974380752951,38.9693930061784],[-109.24992600752921,38.96853620617975],[-109.2498834075293,38.968085806180454],[-109.24896100753074,38.96699887284876],[-109.24748240753303,38.96541227285127],[-109.24527920753644,38.963496672854205],[-109.2451874075366,38.962931006188455],[-109.24511647420337,38.96233787285604],[-109.2448276742038,38.961657072857065],[-109.24418000753815,38.961080672857975],[-109